# PyPI configuration file
.pypirc

# Cursor  
#  Cursor is an AI-powered code editor.`.cursorignore` specifies files/directories to 
#  exclude from AI features like autocomplete and code analysis. Recommended for sensitive data
#  refer to https://docs.cursor.com/context/ignore-files
.cursorignore
.cursorindexingignore

# --- Generated media, samples and job artifacts (DELIBERATELY TRACKED) -----
# By request, the sample clips, dubbed renders, extracted/re-separated audio,
# TTS takes, subtitles and the job directories ARE part of this repo and its
# archive: they are the evidence behind the Phase 7 validation and what a
# reviewer inspects. So media, /jobs, /temp and /output are intentionally NOT
# ignored below. Only true build/runtime caches stay out of the repo.

# --- New runtime output under those trees is NOT tracked -------------------
# The evidence above stays committed: git keeps files that are already tracked
# no matter what these rules say. What the rules do is stop a *fresh* run from
# silently adding to the repository. A render writes dozens of timestamped
# files per job, so without this every run would bury real changes in
# `git status` and invite an accidental commit of gigabytes of intermediates.
# Documentation, runtime output, scratch and samples are not versioned.
/docs
/jobs/*
/temp/*
/output/*
/samples
# Project notes that are not part of the codebase.
REMAINING_PHASES.md
RUNNING.md

